  "title": "Multiplication Closure with a Linear Factor for Normalized Pochhammer Transforms",
  "batch_label": "45",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every real a>0 and all real polynomials P_1,P_2 with deg(P_1)=1 and deg(P_2)=2, if every zero of L_a(P_1) and L_a(P_2) lies in [-1,0], then every zero of L_a(P_1P_2) lies in [-1,0]. More generally, for every n>=0, a>0, and r in [0,1], the operator T_r f=(x+r)f+x(x+1)f'/a maps every degree-n real polynomial whose zeros all lie in [-1,0] to a degree-(n+1) polynomial whose zeros all lie in [-1,0].",
